# Tank Battalion sound circuits -- netlist converted from MAME
#
# Ryan Holtz's netlist of Tank Battalion's discrete sound, which his file says is derived
# from the schematics in the manual. The sound latch bits (S1, S2, OFF, ENGINE_HI, SHOOT,
# HIT) and the video counter's 2V and 4V arrive as ports. MAME reaches into the 7486's
# gates by name (6K.A.Q) and declares the CD4006 without its package; both are put on
# their pins by MAME's own DIP models. The diodes are generic in MAME: 'types not listed
# on schematic'.
#
# Source: MAME mame0289 (commit f34f02505e32), src/mame/namco/nl_tankbatt.cpp,
# NETLIST_START(tankbatt). Licence BSD-3-Clause by the file's own header (line 1),
# copyright-holders Ryan Holtz (line 2).
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mamedev/mame/mame0289/src/mame/namco/nl_tankbatt.cpp
# Converted by tools/mame_netlist.py; checked by tools/build_board_nets.py.
#
# What the conversion means. MAME's netlists are written to be simulated, so this is a
# second reading of the sheet by someone else, not a read of it: designators and pin
# numbers are MAME's unless the notes say the sheet was read to correct them. Names on
# `label` lines are MAME's, which mostly follow the sheet's with Q for an overbar; `net`
# is used only for the supply rails. A `port` is a net that leaves what this file
# describes -- a signal from the CPU or the other board, a cabinet control, or a source
# MAME simulates with a stand-in rather than the circuit.
#
#   net NAME: PIN ...     a supply rail
#   label NAME: PIN ...   a net MAME names
#   wire PIN PIN ...      an unnamed connection
#   port NAME: PIN ...    a net that leaves this file (see above)
#   nc PIN ...            a pin with nothing attached
#   parallel PIN ...      outputs the board sums on one node by design
#   value REF VALUE       a passive's value, in the unit MAME's own macro uses
#
# PIN is DESIGNATOR.NUMBER. Diode pin 1 is the cathode; transistors keep B, C and E;
# MAME does not record which way round an electrolytic goes, so C pins are MAME's 1/2.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Undone: what MAME does to simulate the board that the board does not do
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# line 87: dropped NET_C(VCC, _5K.5, _6F.VDD, _6J.4, _6K.7, _6L.14, S1.VCC, S2.VCC, OFF.VCC, ENGINE_HI.VCC, SHOOT.VCC, HIT.VCC, 2V.VCC, 4V.VCC) -- took _6K.7 out of it: pin 7 of the 7486 at 6K is its ground
# line 88: dropped NET_C(GND, _5K.10, _6F.VSS, _6J.11, _6K.14, _6L.7, S1.GND, S2.GND, OFF.GND, ENGINE_HI.GND, SHOOT.GND, HIT.GND, 2V.GND, 4V.GND) -- took _6K.14 out of it: pin 14 of the 7486 at 6K is its supply
#
# Corrected from the 7486's standard pinout -- the site holds no Tank Battalion PCB schematic:
#   pin 14, the 7486's VCC, on +5V (MAME's lines 87-88 swap its supply pins; its TTL_7486_DIP model does not use them): V5 U6K.14
#   pin 7, the 7486's GND, on ground: U6K.7
# Stand-ins that are not parts (the nets they drive are ports): CLOCK(2V), CLOCK(4V), TTL_INPUT(S1), TTL_INPUT(S2), TTL_INPUT(OFF), TTL_INPUT(ENGINE_HI), TTL_INPUT(SHOOT), TTL_INPUT(HIT)
#
# Left out by MAME (commented out at TAG, so not in this file either):
#   line 43: RES(R41, RES_K(22))
#
# MAME's netlist ends at the summing node of R35, R36, R56_1, R56_2 and R59, so this file
# has no output port of its own; the node is a plain net here. R56 appears twice in MAME
# (R56_1, R56_2), one on each of the hit and shoot channels.
#
# Not compared with the sheet: the site's Tank Battalion manual (doc 73495cc3ecf0, the
# upright service manual) has no PCB schematic -- operation, test, cabinet parts lists,
# the harness (p29) and a block diagram (p30) only (read 2026-10-20); MAME worked from a
# printing that has one. What the manual does show is where the sound goes after this
# file: a volume pot on the PCB (Fig. 5-7), the audio output on J1 pin 18 (the speaker
# check is #18 to Z), a second volume pot behind the coin door on J4 pins 12-14 and the
# speaker on J6, and a 12V AC centre-tapped winding for 'audio power', so a power
# amplifier on the board that MAME does not have. So the 7486 supply fix rests on the
# part's pinout alone, and R46/R49 are MAME's 4.7K against what its own comment says the
# schematic prints (47K).
#
# Not compared with the sheet. MAME's designators, values and pin numbers are taken as
# MAME has them; the checker shows the netlist is internally consistent (every pin exists,
# no two outputs fight, nothing floats), which is not the same as matching the board.

# part U5K 7492  (MAME: _5K)
# part U6F CD4006  (MAME: _6F)
# part U6J LM324  (MAME: _6J)
# part U6K 7486  (MAME: _6K)
# part U6L CD4066  (MAME: _6L)

value R31 470
value R32 470
value R35 4.7K
value R36 4.7K
value R37 6.8K
value R38 10K
value R42 22K
value R43 22K
value R44 33K
value R45 47K
value R46 4.7K  # MAME's comment: 'Possible schematic or scan-quality error: Schematic says 47K'
value R47 4.7K
value R48 4.7K
value R49 4.7K  # MAME's comment: 'Possible schematic or scan-quality error: Schematic says 47K'
value R50 150K
value R51 150K
value R52 220K
value R53 470K
value R54 470K
value R56_1 1K
value R56_2 1K
value R57 10K
value R58 1K
value R59 1K
value R60 1K
value R61 1K
value C10 2.2uF
value C11 2.2uF
value C12 2.2uF
value C13 2.2uF
value C14 0.1uF
value C15 0.01uF
value C16 0.01uF
value C17 0.01uF
value C18 0.01uF
value C42 0.1uF
value D8 D  # MAME's comment: 'Generic diodes, types not listed on schematic'
value D9 D
value D10 D
value D11 D

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supplies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
net GND: C10.2 C11.2 C12.2 C13.2 C14.2 R37.2 R42.2 R43.2 R48.2 R57.2 U5K.10 U6F.7 U6J.11 U6K.7 U6L.7
net +5V: R44.2 R47.2 U5K.5 U5K.7 U6F.14 U6J.4 U6K.10 U6K.14 U6L.14

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Noise generation (presumably)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port 2V: U6F.3 U6L.1  # in MAME: CLOCK(2V)
wire U6F.13 U6F.5
wire U6F.10 U6F.6 U6L.12 U6L.6
wire U6F.1 U6F.12 U6K.1
wire U6F.8 U6K.2
wire R38.1 U6K.3
wire D9.1 R38.2 U6F.4
wire D8.2 R53.1 U6F.9
wire C42.1 D8.1 R53.2 U6J.2
wire C42.2 D9.2 U6J.1
wire C12.1 R43.1 R44.1 U6J.10 U6J.12 U6J.3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# S1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port S1: U6L.5  # in MAME: TTL_INPUT(S1)
port 4V: U6L.4  # in MAME: CLOCK(4V)
wire R35.1 U6L.3

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# S2
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port S2: U6L.13  # in MAME: TTL_INPUT(S2)
wire R36.1 U6L.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hit
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port HIT: R31.1  # in MAME: TTL_INPUT(HIT)
wire D10.2 R31.2
wire C10.1 D10.1 U6L.8
wire R50.1 U6L.9
wire C15.1 C16.1 R42.1 R50.2
wire C16.2 R54.1 U6J.9
wire C15.2 R54.2 R56_1.1 U6J.8

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shoot
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port SHOOT: R32.1  # in MAME: TTL_INPUT(SHOOT)
wire D11.2 R32.2
wire C11.1 D11.1 U6L.11
wire R45.1 U6L.10
wire C17.1 C18.1 R37.1 R45.2
wire C18.2 R51.1 U6J.13
wire C17.2 R51.2 R56_2.1 U6J.14

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Engine Rumble
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
port ENGINE_HI: U6K.4  # in MAME: TTL_INPUT(ENGINE_HI)
wire U6K.5 U6K.8
wire R52.1 U5K.1 U6K.6
wire C14.1 R46.1 R52.2 U6J.6
wire R47.1 R48.1 R49.1 U6J.5
wire R46.2 R49.2 R57.1 U6J.7 U6K.9
port OFF: U5K.6  # in MAME: TTL_INPUT(OFF)
wire R60.1 U5K.11 U6K.12
wire R58.1 U5K.8 U6K.13
wire U5K.14 U6K.11
wire R61.1 U5K.12
wire C13.1 R58.2 R59.1 R60.2 R61.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mixing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
wire R35.2 R36.2 R56_1.2 R56_2.2 R59.2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins with nothing attached
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pins the MAME netlist never mentions. On a real board these are unused outputs, or
# inputs left open or tied in a way MAME did not draw; they are written here so that
# the checker's coverage test still means something for every other pin.
nc U5K.9  # Q2
nc U6F.2 U6F.11  # NC D2+4
